<title>UK: United News dips, Blenheim up on bid news.</title>
<headline>United News dips, Blenheim up on bid news.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in United News &amp; Media Plc were marked lower in early trading on Tuesday after the company said it had taken control of Blenheim Group Plc after weeks of bid speculation around the exhibition organiser.</p>
<p>United News shares were down 4p at 649-1/2 by 0703 GMT while Blenheim rose 26-1/2p to 500.  </p>
<p>United said it made an agreed 500p per share cash bid for Blenheim, valuing the target at 592.5 million stg, and had acceptances or owned 51 percent of Blenheim shares.  </p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
